# Retry design with incomplete evidence

Plan a cancellable retry mechanism for idempotent GET requests in a Node.js client. The selected
contract requires independent per-request attempt budgets and the existing overall deadline;
POST must never be retried automatically. We have no retry helper or installed retry dependency,
and no verified reference implementation. The transport already accepts AbortSignal. A retained
platform API record documents that the timer primitive accepts a signal and rejects on abort.

External repositories and live documentation are inaccessible in this environment. No copied
source, license text, maintenance history, tests or issue records are available for candidate
libraries. Local investigation found no other applicable implementation. The team is unfamiliar
with cancellation across both transport and backoff. Provide a provisional design and identify
the evidence or experiments needed before adoption. Implementation and dependency changes are
outside this task. Do not invent upstream facts or claim that experiments have run.
